From: Charles Keepax <ckeepax@opensource.cirrus.com>
Date: Wed, 8 Jul 2026 13:29:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: intel_auxdevice: Add cs42l44 to wake_capable_list
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.61
Git-commit: d08e4d9197396ceb906715d976b63aed0c5cc8e5

[ Upstream commit d08e4d9197396ceb906715d976b63aed0c5cc8e5 ]

Add cs42l44 to the wake_capable_list because it can generate
jack events whilst the bus is stopped.

Signed-off-by: Charles Keepax <ckeepax@opensource.cirrus.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260708122948.1502227-1-ckeepax@opensource.cirrus.com
Signed-off-by: Vinod Koul <vkoul@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 drivers/soundwire/intel_auxdevice.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/intel_auxdevice.c b/drivers/soundwire/intel_auxdevice.c
index c0c8ffcecc6b..347e06ad6edb 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/intel_auxdevice.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/intel_auxdevice.c
@@ -54,6 +54,7 @@ static struct wake_capable_part wake_capable_list[] = {
 	{0x01fa, 0x2A30},
 	{0x01fa, 0x2A3B},
 	{0x01fa, 0x4243},
+	{0x01fa, 0x4244},
 	{0x01fa, 0x4245},
 	{0x025d, 0x5682},
 	{0x025d, 0x700},
-- 
